+// (ENGINE-VISION2 V4, patches/metal-imrope.patch) IMRoPE. The rope kernels' pos
+// is the KV SLOT (the cache row written and the causal bound); the rope ANGLE
+// takes the position LLB_MRP(A, slot, t) of rotary pair t (sector t % 3: 0 t,
+// 1 h, 2 w; ggml's imrope with sections [11, 11, 10], every t < 32 inside
+// them). mr = {s0, n, nx, sh}: one image of n rows at slots s0 .. s0 + n - 1 in
+// raster order of width nx gets (t, h, w) = (s0, s0 + i / nx, s0 + i % nx)
+// (mtmd's MTMD_POS_TYPE_MROPE, i = slot - s0); slots after it resume at
+// slot - sh (sh = n - max(nx, ny): mtmd's n_pos); slots before it are
+// themselves. mr[1] == 0 (every text-only run: m9_args / f27_targs copy the
+// host's llb_mr, zero unless an image prompt set it) is the slot in all three
+// sectors, the expression the kernels had
+#define LLB_MRP(A, s, t) ((A).mr[1] == 0 || (s) < (A).mr[0] ? (s) \
+  : (s) - (A).mr[0] >= (A).mr[1] ? (s) - (A).mr[3] \
+  : (t) % 3 == 0 ? (A).mr[0] \
+  : (t) % 3 == 1 ? (A).mr[0] + ((s) - (A).mr[0]) / (A).mr[2] \
+  : (A).mr[0] + ((s) - (A).mr[0]) % (A).mr[2])
 
